/**
@page contributing Contributing

@tableofcontents

@section contributing_read_first Read first

* `README.md` — user-facing overview and quick start.
* `HACKING` — coding style, naming rules, and the generated-file boundary.
* `HACKING_COMMON_DOC` — checklist for adding a new WCH family.
* `NOTICE` — provenance and licence rules; read it before importing anything.

@section contributing_rules Hard rules

1. Use lower-case `periph_verb_noun()` names, not WCH EVT CamelCase.
2. Do not copy WCH EVT code.  WCH's EVT and ch32fun are reference material for
   register facts, not source.
3. Keep the build system libopencm3-shaped: `TARGETS` recursion, `mk/`
   modules, `ld/devices.data`, `genlink.py`, and `irq.json`.
4. One archive per family.  Never mix RV32EC and RV32IMAC objects in one
   archive.
5. CH58x RWA registers must go through the unlock/lock safe-access helpers.
6. Do not hand-edit generated `nvic.h` or `vector_*.c` files.
7. Run `clang-format`; `checkpatch.pl` is only a second opinion.
8. New public API must be registered in the WCH-EVT-to-libopenwch mapping
   table and documented in a Doxygen group.

@section contributing_flow Suggested flow

@code
make clean && make
make genlinktests
make apitest
make stylecheck
make html
@endcode

Check that `doc/doxygen-root.log` and `doc/<family>/doxygen.log` are empty,
and open the generated HTML before declaring documentation work complete.

@section contributing_commits Commit messages

Use `<area>: <imperative summary>` (for example `gpio: add alternate-function
selection`).  Keep one logical change per commit.  The generated HTML output
and build archives are not committed.

@section contributing_repos Repository map

The library is only one of four repositories; changes that affect the
application skeleton, examples, or flasher belong in their own repositories:

* <a href="https://github.com/LrkSeraph/libopenwch">libopenwch</a> — driver library.
* <a href="https://github.com/LrkSeraph/libopenwch-template">libopenwch-template</a> — app skeleton.
* <a href="https://github.com/LrkSeraph/libopenwch-examples">libopenwch-examples</a> — worked examples.
* <a href="https://github.com/LrkSeraph/libopenwch-tools">libopenwch-tools</a> — `wchlink` host tool.
*/
